API Calls: Promises and Fetches with JSON files/servers

AKA: Why there's a bicycle on the highway

without the API Online you can't make any calls (why websites always have a server running)

first you need to download json-server


when you do api calls there are 3 statuses to promises: fulfilled, rejected, pending

so long as it's pending, you're not getting any information

rejected promises almost always have a html error code (usually 500 unauthenticated)

fulfilled promises give usually a html code 200 (ok)

json servers are stored normally on the localhost, but each port can only be opened 1 time, so if one
is on localhost:3000, the next one should be on 3001.

in the server directory, write json-server --watch (json file here) to start up a json server
